        "discipline": "running",
        "description": "As an experienced runner, you probably already do a long run of around 60-90 minutes on the weekends anyway. The schedule suggests an increase in distance as you get closer to race date: from 5 to 13 miles. Don't get hung up on running these workouts too fast. Run at a comfortable, conversational pace 15 to 90. If Sunday isn't a convenient day for your long runs, feel free to do them on Saturday-or any other day of the week for that matter.",
